CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ out-of-line pack body runs: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member updated: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.mem.func] + [temp.inst]/2: an out-of-line-defined member function
template of a class template is instantiated from its definition.  Fixed by
attaching the definition's body (recorded as a template_methods entry of the
enclosing class template, with the owning class matched to avoid same-name
cross-template adoption) to the instantiated member-template declarator, and
switching to the definition's parameter names ([dcl.fct]/3).  Runtime-verified
against g++ and clang++.
